From a77cd7eae8fbb46d2e39f019444cb1ddee777a37 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Neivin Detlefsen <neivin.detlefsen@gmx.de>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 21:34:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] fix: read the mode 2 offset-per-tile rows at bg3vofs
 and bg3vofs + 8

PpuDrawBackground_4bpp_opt took snes9x's `VOffset - 1` and
`VCellOffset + 1` over to the raw BGnVOFS value in vScroll[] and to the
1-based line y. snes9x keeps BGnVOFS + 1 per line and counts lines from
0, so both corrections came out one line off here: the H row was read
at BG3VOFS - 1 and the V row at BG3VOFS + 7, and an offset column
showed row entry + 1 + y instead of entry + y.

With BG3VOFS = 0 the V offsets came from the H row. FF6's battle Slot
reels (Mode 2, OPT map at $8000) stood still at offset 0, although OPT
table, HDMA and registers matched snes9x; with the fix the frame is
pixel-equal to the reference. The H column (`hscroll + x - 1`) already
matches snes9x and stays as it is.

Regression: tests/ppu/ppu_mode2_opt_test.c (BG3VOFS 0, 8 and 12).
